  "result": "`Math.random` is implemented in `crates/kahvi-builtins/src/math/random.rs`, and `./t262 built-ins/Math/random/` now passes 10 of 10 (up from 8 on main). Clippy is clean and the file passes `cargo fmt --check`.\n\nThe engine had no RNG and no `rand` dependency, so I used a SplitMix64 stream seeded from std's `RandomState`. All realms draw from that one stream, so their sequences differ. The result is the top 53 bits scaled by 2^-53, which lies in [0, 1). Making each realm hold its own generator would need a field on the realm in `kahvi-core`, which is outside this ticket's scope.\n\nBLOCKED: none",
